  * Migration 120 (mfa_factors): user_mfa, webauthn_credentials, totp_factors,
    recovery_code_batches, recovery_codes; additive and idempotent (#356).
  * auth::mfa factor storage: RFC 6238 TOTP (SHA-1, 6 digits, 30 s, window +-1)
    with seeds AES-256-GCM sealed under mfa_seal (AAD binds user and factor)
    and a conditional-UPDATE replay guard; unconfirmed enrollments expire after
    10 minutes (Janitor purge).
  * Recovery codes: 10 x 50-bit Crockford codes, keyed BLAKE2b-256 under
    mfa_pepper, batch inactive until acknowledged and superseding the previous
    one, single use by conditional UPDATE.
  * crypto::secrets::Manager::sealedKey: seal-and-read-back internal keys that
    fail closed and are never regenerated while dependents exist
    (secrets::dependents::mfaSeal/mfaPepper).
  * vh secrets export accepts mfa-seal and mfa-pepper (base64); ws log
    redaction covers MFA codes, otpauth URIs and WebAuthn material.
  * Pending-MFA sign-in (#357): a correct password for an account with a usable
    factor, or one the MFA policy requires one of, leaves the socket pending
    (no session user, access token or refresh row) instead of signing in;
    auth.login answers mfa_required / mfa_enrollment_required with
    data.pending.
  * Router pending mode with an exact allowlist (auth.mfa.verify,
    auth.mfa.cancel, auth.logout, plus the enrollment commands while
    enrolling); it ends after 5 min (10 enrolling), 5 failed factors, cancel,
    logout or the socket closing. Account-wide cap: 5 factor failures in 15 min
    answer rate_limited.
  * auth::mfa::policy at level admins (D2): an aal 1 refresh row of an account
    that must have MFA is revoked and refused at next use; installed at startup
    through the session assurance hook.
  * New ws commands auth.mfa.verify, auth.mfa.cancel, auth.mfa.status,
    auth.mfa.webauthn.register.options|finish,
