    `CloudRemoteReadTest.Vhf1*`.
  * Encrypted metadata manifest v2 for `opaque_v1` vaults (#368, WS3-a;
    design/encryption/03 §3-§4): a copy-on-write root (VHF1 kind 3,
    epoch-chained, pinning segments by SHA-256 and size) and uid-partitioned
    segments (VHF1 kind 2) carrying the tree, trash, tombstones, provider
    versions, prior names, snapshot records and the key history with
    attestations; segments are written with `If-None-Match: *`, the root with
    `If-Match`, a 412 is merged, never overwritten; garbage collection keeps
    the last three roots' segments. Readers apply the rollback/fork/gap chain
    rules with provider-version and older-root fallbacks and a blind
    header-only rebuild floor. `opaque_v1` stays test mode only (#371);
    `path_v0` and `transparent` vaults keep `index-v1.json` unchanged.
  * Migration 125: `remote_manifest_state` gains `epoch`, `root_sha256`, the
    refused root (`refused_reason`, `refused_epoch`, `refused_root_sha256`,
    `refused_at`) and `gc_at`; new `remote_manifest_root` (sids of the last
    three roots); `directories.uid` and `symlinks.uid` (libsodium uids assigned
    by the manifest collector, immutable); `files_trashed.object_uid` (set when
