vaulthalla (1.18.0-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Source moved to github.com/valkyrianlabs/vaulthalla-server (Homepage,
    debian/copyright Source, release.toml); the old vaulthalla/server URLs
    redirect. CI runs on the Valkyrian Labs VPS build pool (label vps-ci).
  * The macOS installer's Nexus mirror moved to the valkyrian-raw repository
    (pkg.vaulthalla.sh).
  * S3 gateway: a signed content-length that a proxy stripped (Cloudflare drops
    Content-Length: 0) is canonicalized as 0 when the request has no body and
    no Transfer-Encoding; every response sends Cache-Control: private,
    no-store.
  * TPM sealer: seal/unseal are serialized per process (each holds 2 of the
    TPM's 3 transient object slots; the swtpm TCTI has no resource manager), so
    concurrent unseals no longer fail Esys_Load with TPM_RC_OBJECT_MEMORY;
    transient TPM warnings (object/session memory, retry, yielded, testing) are
    retried up to 5 times with backoff.
  * Stats: rollup retention is configurable per tier
    (stats_snapshots.rollup_5m_retention_days, default 30;
    rollup_1h_retention_days, default 365, never below the 5-minute value)
    instead of a hard-coded 365 days for both; the purge logs how many rows it
    deleted. Operator docs describe a one-time VACUUM (FULL) / pg_repack.

