vaulthalla (1.17.0-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Durability
    - Durability flushes go through `platform::durable::sync`: `fsync` on Linux
      (unchanged), `F_FULLFSYNC` on macOS (falling back to `fsync` only where
      the file system refuses it). A contract test rejects raw `fsync` outside
      `core/src/platform/` (#205).
  * File API
    - fs entries (ws `fs.dir.list` / `fs.list` / `fs.metadata`, sync conflict
      artifacts) carry `metadata_version` (all entries) and `content_version`
      (files), set by the Entry base serializer (#257).
      + `content_version` = `storage::Generation::etag()`, the strong ETag
        `/download/content` serves; it changes on every content write, never on
        rename or move.
      + `metadata_version` =
        `"m<id>-<hex16(sha256(vault|parent|name|mode|owner|group|updated_at))>"`,
        a stable hash of the fields the reply carries (no counter, no
        migration).
      + An empty file's generation is `plain:0` whatever its `updated_at`, so
        its ETag survives rename and touch.
      + `FsEntryVersionsDbTest`: the entry id is unchanged across ws rename, ws
        move, FUSE rename over an existing file and a folder move (its children
        too).
    - `PUT /upload/content?vault_id&path` (#258,
      `protocols/http/upload/Content.cpp`): conditional replace (`If-Match`,
      `Need::Overwrite`) or create (`If-None-Match: *`,
      `access::resolveCreate`: Write) of one file, body streamed by
      `Session::handle_streaming_content` into the upload staging seam and
      sealed through
      `Filesystem::createFile{source_path, overwrite, expected_source_id}`.
      + 412 + current ETag on a stale version, an open FUSE working copy or an
        existing file on create; 409 for a non-file in the way; 428 / 411 / 413
        answered before the body; access checked again at commit.
      + 201/200 answer `{created, entry}` with `content_version` /
        `metadata_version` and the new ETag.
    - `/upload/session` commits seal from the staged file (`source_path`)
      instead of reading it whole into memory; an empty file keeps the
      empty-buffer branch (same MIME type). A file whose PUT failed may be PUT
      again (human and device sessions; a share upload's record stays failed).
    - `tools/contracts/test_upload_content_contract.py` pins the bounded-memory
      commit and the streaming route.
  * Security
    - ws `fs.dir.list` / `fs.list` (outside share mode) and `vh fs ls` leave
      out children the caller cannot Lookup, through the filter FUSE readdir
      uses (`rbac::fs::visibility`), and recount a listed child folder's size
      and counts and the folder's own size without them (#255).
    - The listing fast path no longer skips the per-entry Lookup when a
      wildcard override reaches the folder from above
      (`glob::Matcher::mayMatchWithin`) or when the base permissions hide one
      kind of entry.
    - FUSE rename and ws `fs.entry.move` / `fs.entry.rename` into another
      folder authorize the new path with the action a create there needs (Touch
      for a folder, Write for a file or symlink; `rbac::fs::placement`), and
      every entry a folder carries at its new path. FUSE answers a refusal as a
      create in that folder would (`resolver::deniedErrno`), ws with `denied`
      before any destination lookup. Same-folder renames and cross-vault EXDEV
      are unchanged (#256).
  * Test tooling
    - `make test` runs the derive suites: `vh_fake_derive_helper` is built
      without sanitizers (an ASan helper aborted under the Runner's RLIMIT_AS
      cap), so DeriveRunnerTest and DeriveQueueDbTest pass in the sanitized
      build-itest.
    - `make test` works on macOS: it builds with tools/macos/env.sh and runs
      vh_unit_tests against a disposable per-run PostgreSQL cluster
      (tools/macos/test-db.sh), torn down afterwards; `make itest` exits early
      there with what to run. Test scripts drop GNU-only `realpath -m`,
      `base64 -w0`, `mapfile` and `declare -A` (bash 3.2 compatible), and the
      harness provisioner accepts /tmp as /private/tmp.
  * macOS mount
    - Retire the macOS macFUSE integration (#262): darwin never builds the
      kernel FUSE bridge (`-Dfuse=enabled` is a setup error there;
      `fuse/unbuilt` is the service), `platform/darwin/Mount.cpp` drops the
      macFUSE mount options, the `fuse_session_mount` probe and the
      `macfuse-kernel` backend, and `tools/macos/fuse-probe/` is removed.
      Finder access belongs to Vaulthalla Desktop's File Provider
      (vaulthalla/desktop#1). Linux FUSE is unchanged.
      + macOS `mount.mode` is `disabled` only: `service_private`/`multiuser`
        left in config.yaml run as `disabled` with a `[config]` warning instead
        of degrading health; a misspelled mode still refuses to start
        everywhere.
      + Health, `vh status` and the console's Runtime page report the macOS
        mount as disabled, noting that Finder access is provided by Vaulthalla
        Desktop. `vh fs` help no longer calls itself interim.
  * Packaging
    - Valkyrian Labs LLC is the copyright holder and trademark owner: `NOTICE`,
      `TRADEMARKS.md`, `debian/copyright` (`Upstream-Contact` and both `Files`
      stanzas), `debian/copyright_human`, the README and CONTRIBUTING say so.
      `debian/copyright` now also lists the vendored jwt-cpp, nlohmann/json,
      picojson and stb headers under their own licenses.
    - The repository moved to `github.com/vaulthalla/server`. The package
      `Homepage`/`Source` fields (`debian/control`, `debian/copyright`), the
      release contract (`release.toml`), the Homebrew cask URL and the docs
      links point there; the old `vaulthalla-core` and `vaulthalla/vaulthalla`
      URLs are gone.
    - Published to the Valkyrian Labs APT repository (`release.toml`
      `[publish.apt].repository_url` = `https://apt.valkyrianlabs.com`;
      Production `NEXUS_REPO_URL` likewise); `apt.vaulthalla.sh` is an nginx
      alias of the same Nexus repo. The publish job shares the
      `valkyrianlabs-apt-publish` concurrency group with the other publishers.
    - `Recommends: valkyrianlabs-archive-keyring` (vl-release refuses a Depends
      on it). `Depends: vaulthalla-archive-keyring` stays: from 2026.10.27-1 it
      ships the Valkyrian Labs LLC key (and, during the move, the retiring
      Vaulthalla key) at `/usr/share/keyrings/vaulthalla.gpg`.
    - `bin/vh/install.sh` and `bin/setup/install_deps.sh` configure
      `apt.valkyrianlabs.com` with `/usr/share/keyrings/valkyrianlabs.gpg` and
      retire an unchanged `vaulthalla.list` they wrote earlier; install.sh
      skips its own source when another file already names the repository. The
      CI image uses the one source.

